{"videoId":"TB8E2HZ47as","source":"auto","lang":"en","sentences":[{"start":0.0,"end":3.24,"text":"This is the only video you need"},{"start":3.24,"end":4.4,"text":"to master"},{"start":4.4,"end":5.32,"text":"the present"},{"start":5.32,"end":6.2,"text":"tenses"},{"start":6.2,"end":7.16,"text":"in English."},{"start":7.16,"end":10.8,"text":"I will teach them to you in just 11"},{"start":10.8,"end":11.64,"text":"minutes."},{"start":11.64,"end":12.76,"text":"We will cover"},{"start":12.76,"end":14.64,"text":"the present simple."},{"start":14.64,"end":16.24,"text":"I teach."},{"start":16.24,"end":18.4,"text":"The present continuous."},{"start":18.4,"end":20.4,"text":"I'm teaching."},{"start":20.4,"end":21.92,"text":"The present perfect"},{"start":21.92,"end":23.4,"text":"simple."},{"start":23.4,"end":25.44,"text":"I've taught."},{"start":25.44,"end":26.52,"text":"And the present"},{"start":26.52,"end":28.72,"text":"perfect continuous."},{"start":28.72,"end":30.12,"text":"I've been"},{"start":30.12,"end":30.88,"text":"teaching."},{"start":30.88,"end":34.84,"text":">> Want to know the secret to speaking English with real confidence?"},{"start":34.84,"end":35.92,"text":"It's mastering"},{"start":35.92,"end":37.04,"text":"the tenses."},{"start":37.04,"end":40.88,"text":"Once you fully understand them, you'll know with certainty"},{"start":40.88,"end":46.84,"text":"that you're speaking correctly. Trust me, it's the best feeling. And because it's so important,"},{"start":46.84,"end":48.84,"text":"I've made something incredibly"},{"start":48.84,"end":50.72,"text":"special that you can download"},{"start":50.72,"end":56.96,"text":"for free. It's an ebook complete with all the English tenses in one place. Past,"},{"start":56.96,"end":58.36,"text":"present, future,"},{"start":58.36,"end":59.64,"text":"and conditional."},{"start":59.64,"end":64.28,"text":"All of it. Inside, you'll find clear, simple explanations,"},{"start":64.28,"end":65.96,"text":"loads of examples,"},{"start":65.96,"end":67.56,"text":"and quizzes to practice."},{"start":67.56,"end":70.08,"text":"This ebook is one of the best resources"},{"start":70.08,"end":72.12,"text":"I've made for English learners."},{"start":72.12,"end":77.24,"text":"And right now, it's free. Click the link below or scan the QR code on screen."},{"start":77.24,"end":80.0,"text":"Just enter your name and email address,"},{"start":80.0,"end":84.2,"text":"join my mailing list, and I'll send the ebook straight to your inbox."},{"start":84.2,"end":88.64,"text":"You'll also get all my future YouTube lessons and free PDFs,"},{"start":88.64,"end":93.12,"text":"along with news about my courses and special offers. It's a free service, and you can"},{"start":93.12,"end":93.84,"text":"unsubscribe"},{"start":93.84,"end":99.52,"text":"at any time. Download the ebook today. It's yours forever. Right, let's get started with the"},{"start":99.52,"end":102.8,"text":"video. >> Let's begin with the present simple."},{"start":102.8,"end":104.16,"text":"I teach."},{"start":104.16,"end":107.72,"text":"We use this tense to talk about things that are true"},{"start":107.72,"end":109.56,"text":"or facts."},{"start":109.56,"end":110.8,"text":"For example,"},{"start":110.8,"end":112.4,"text":"my dog's name"},{"start":112.4,"end":114.68,"text":"is Diego."},{"start":114.68,"end":116.24,"text":"Or I don't"},{"start":116.24,"end":118.88,"text":"have brown hair."},{"start":118.88,"end":120.6,"text":"Or I speak"},{"start":120.6,"end":121.68,"text":"Spanish"},{"start":121.68,"end":122.64,"text":"fluently."},{"start":122.64,"end":126.12,"text":"We also use it for things that happen regularly,"},{"start":126.12,"end":127.48,"text":"like habits"},{"start":127.48,"end":129.64,"text":"and routines."},{"start":129.64,"end":131.0,"text":"I release"},{"start":131.0,"end":132.64,"text":"a new video"},{"start":132.64,"end":136.84,"text":"every week. We often use the present simple with expressions"},{"start":136.84,"end":137.88,"text":"of frequency,"},{"start":137.88,"end":140.2,"text":"such as every week,"},{"start":140.2,"end":142.0,"text":"every Saturday,"},{"start":142.0,"end":144.08,"text":"three times a month,"},{"start":144.08,"end":145.48,"text":"and so on."},{"start":145.48,"end":146.6,"text":"These expressions"},{"start":146.6,"end":149.16,"text":"usually go at the end of a sentence,"},{"start":149.16,"end":152.4,"text":"but we can sometimes put them at the beginning."},{"start":152.4,"end":153.64,"text":"Every week,"},{"start":153.64,"end":156.28,"text":"I release a new video."},{"start":156.28,"end":158.32,"text":"Now, adverbs of frequency,"},{"start":158.32,"end":160.0,"text":"like always,"},{"start":160.0,"end":161.0,"text":"usually,"},{"start":161.0,"end":161.96,"text":"sometimes,"},{"start":161.96,"end":163.68,"text":"and rarely,"},{"start":163.68,"end":165.56,"text":"generally go before"},{"start":165.56,"end":166.72,"text":"the main verb,"},{"start":166.72,"end":167.44,"text":"but"},{"start":167.44,"end":168.2,"text":"after"},{"start":168.2,"end":171.12,"text":"the verb to be, such as I"},{"start":171.12,"end":171.88,"text":"always"},{"start":171.88,"end":174.8,"text":"go for a run in the morning, and"},{"start":174.8,"end":176.2,"text":"I am"},{"start":176.2,"end":177.28,"text":"never"},{"start":177.28,"end":179.16,"text":"late for meetings."},{"start":179.16,"end":182.04,"text":"Don't forget to add an S or ES"},{"start":182.04,"end":186.36,"text":"to positive verbs with the subjects he, she, and it."},{"start":186.36,"end":189.68,"text":"This is a very common error with the present simple,"},{"start":189.68,"end":191.88,"text":"even for high-level learners."},{"start":191.88,"end":193.0,"text":"An example,"},{"start":193.0,"end":194.12,"text":"Diego"},{"start":194.12,"end":195.04,"text":"loves"},{"start":195.04,"end":197.12,"text":"walking on the beach."},{"start":197.12,"end":198.0,"text":"Heather"},{"start":198.0,"end":199.2,"text":"watches"},{"start":199.2,"end":201.08,"text":"TV in the evening."},{"start":201.08,"end":204.44,"text":"Use does not or the short form doesn't,"},{"start":204.44,"end":207.56,"text":"plus the base verb, to make negatives"},{"start":207.56,"end":211.12,"text":"with he, she, and it. For all other subjects,"},{"start":211.12,"end":212.84,"text":"use don't."},{"start":212.84,"end":215.72,"text":"They don't like big cities."},{"start":215.72,"end":217.4,"text":"And the question form?"},{"start":217.4,"end":220.16,"text":"Well, with he, she, and it, use"},{"start":220.16,"end":221.16,"text":"does"},{"start":221.16,"end":222.24,"text":"subject"},{"start":222.24,"end":223.56,"text":"base verb."},{"start":223.56,"end":225.64,"text":"Does she like"},{"start":225.64,"end":226.48,"text":"cats?"},{"start":226.48,"end":227.92,"text":"With all other subjects,"},{"start":227.92,"end":230.12,"text":"I, you, we, they,"},{"start":230.12,"end":232.52,"text":"use do. Do you eat"},{"start":232.52,"end":233.32,"text":"meat?"},{"start":233.32,"end":236.6,"text":"If there is a question word, put it at the beginning."},{"start":236.6,"end":238.96,"text":"Where does your sister work?"},{"start":238.96,"end":244.8,"text":"Who do you live with? Okay, first tense done. Let's move on to the present continuous,"},{"start":244.8,"end":247.64,"text":"also known as the present progressive."},{"start":247.64,"end":252.44,"text":"We use this tense for things happening now, at the moment of speaking."},{"start":252.44,"end":253.92,"text":"I'm teaching"},{"start":253.92,"end":255.04,"text":"right now."},{"start":255.04,"end":257.0,"text":"You are currently watching"},{"start":257.0,"end":259.96,"text":"this video, or things happening around"},{"start":259.96,"end":261.04,"text":"now."},{"start":261.04,"end":262.32,"text":"Are you watching"},{"start":262.32,"end":263.56,"text":"any good series"},{"start":263.56,"end":264.72,"text":"at the moment?"},{"start":264.72,"end":268.68,"text":"We often use phrases like now, right now, currently,"},{"start":268.68,"end":269.76,"text":"and at the moment"},{"start":269.76,"end":272.12,"text":"with the present continuous."},{"start":272.12,"end":274.84,"text":"Let's compare a couple of sentences."},{"start":274.84,"end":278.36,"text":"I often watch Spanish TV shows."},{"start":278.36,"end":279.68,"text":"This is a habitual"},{"start":279.68,"end":282.44,"text":"action with the present simple."},{"start":282.44,"end":283.84,"text":"I'm watching"},{"start":283.84,"end":287.88,"text":"a great Spanish TV show at the moment."},{"start":287.88,"end":290.0,"text":"This is a temporary action"},{"start":290.0,"end":292.52,"text":"happening around the time of speaking."},{"start":292.52,"end":294.12,"text":"Two more examples."},{"start":294.12,"end":296.72,"text":"Sarah works at the uni."},{"start":296.72,"end":302.4,"text":"This is permanent. She works there all year round. Uni is short for university."},{"start":302.4,"end":303.24,"text":"Will's"},{"start":303.24,"end":304.96,"text":"working on the uni's"},{"start":304.96,"end":306.64,"text":"summer program."},{"start":306.64,"end":308.24,"text":"This is a temporary"},{"start":308.24,"end":309.52,"text":"situation"},{"start":309.52,"end":311.28,"text":"just for the summer months."},{"start":311.28,"end":315.08,"text":"Use the present continuous with action verbs happening now."},{"start":315.08,"end":316.64,"text":"Dad isn't sleeping,"},{"start":316.64,"end":318.48,"text":"he's watching TV."},{"start":318.48,"end":319.24,"text":"But,"},{"start":319.24,"end":323.04,"text":"don't use it with state verbs, which describe states"},{"start":323.04,"end":324.28,"text":"or feelings,"},{"start":324.28,"end":326.44,"text":"and include verbs like agree,"},{"start":326.44,"end":327.2,"text":"believe,"},{"start":327.2,"end":329.12,"text":"need, and prefer."},{"start":329.12,"end":329.92,"text":"I'm"},{"start":329.92,"end":332.4,"text":"having a brother, for example,"},{"start":332.4,"end":333.92,"text":"is not correct."},{"start":333.92,"end":336.84,"text":"We need to say I have a brother."},{"start":336.84,"end":339.44,"text":"We don't say we are preferring"},{"start":339.44,"end":340.88,"text":"living in the countryside"},{"start":340.88,"end":341.72,"text":"now."},{"start":341.72,"end":343.72,"text":"It's we prefer"},{"start":343.72,"end":345.0,"text":"living in the countryside"},{"start":345.0,"end":345.84,"text":"now."},{"start":345.84,"end":352.2,"text":"We also generally use the present continuous to describe what's happening in a picture or photograph."},{"start":352.2,"end":354.36,"text":"It looks like they're studying"},{"start":354.36,"end":356.0,"text":"for an important exam."},{"start":356.0,"end":361.2,"text":"And finally, we can use the present continuous to talk about future arrangements."},{"start":361.2,"end":364.24,"text":"We usually know the day, time, and place"},{"start":364.24,"end":366.4,"text":"even if we don't say them."},{"start":366.4,"end":370.12,"text":"We're getting married in Crete this spring."},{"start":370.12,"end":373.8,"text":"I'm meeting Ali for coffee on Friday."},{"start":373.8,"end":377.08,"text":"Imran's not staying at ours this weekend."},{"start":377.08,"end":380.6,"text":"Now, don't forget the verb to be when forming this tense."},{"start":380.6,"end":383.72,"text":"Lots of learners tend to miss it and say,"},{"start":383.72,"end":388.04,"text":"\"Joe arriving at 6:00.\" or \"We making pancakes.\""},{"start":388.04,"end":390.16,"text":"It should be Joe's arriving."},{"start":390.16,"end":392.0,"text":"We're making."},{"start":392.0,"end":394.48,"text":"Use the contracted forms Joe's"},{"start":394.48,"end":395.72,"text":"and we're"},{"start":395.72,"end":399.84,"text":"instead of Joe is and we are to sound more natural."},{"start":399.84,"end":402.68,"text":"Okay, let's move on to the present perfect simple."},{"start":402.68,"end":404.76,"text":"I have taught."},{"start":404.76,"end":409.16,"text":"We use the present perfect to talk about life experiences."},{"start":409.16,"end":411.88,"text":"Have you ever been to Sri Lanka?"},{"start":411.88,"end":414.92,"text":"I've never broken a bone."},{"start":414.92,"end":417.84,"text":"We use ever in questions and it means"},{"start":417.84,"end":420.04,"text":"at any time in your life."},{"start":420.04,"end":422.08,"text":"We use never with a positive"},{"start":422.08,"end":425.2,"text":"verb to make the sentence negative."},{"start":425.2,"end":430.6,"text":"Notice how it's have you ever been to Sri Lanka, not in."},{"start":430.6,"end":433.88,"text":"That's a very common mistake with the present perfect."},{"start":433.88,"end":438.0,"text":"We can't use the present perfect with a finished time reference."},{"start":438.0,"end":440.2,"text":"To say when something happened,"},{"start":440.2,"end":441.84,"text":"use the past simple."},{"start":441.84,"end":442.84,"text":"For example,"},{"start":442.84,"end":446.0,"text":"\"They've bought a new car last week.\""},{"start":446.0,"end":448.28,"text":"is not correct. \"They bought"},{"start":448.28,"end":452.84,"text":"past simple a new car last week.\" Now, we do use the present perfect"},{"start":452.84,"end":454.72,"text":"to say how many times"},{"start":454.72,"end":456.24,"text":"something has happened"},{"start":456.24,"end":457.88,"text":"up to now. \"Kim's"},{"start":457.88,"end":459.76,"text":"failed her driving test"},{"start":459.76,"end":461.08,"text":"four times.\""},{"start":461.08,"end":463.04,"text":"Don't forget to use has"},{"start":463.04,"end":465.16,"text":"plus past participle"},{"start":465.16,"end":469.2,"text":"with he, she, and it. Kim has failed."},{"start":469.2,"end":473.76,"text":"The present perfect is also used to talk about recent past actions."},{"start":473.76,"end":478.92,"text":"We can add just to emphasize that something happened a very short time ago."},{"start":478.92,"end":481.68,"text":"You've missed Sally, I'm afraid."},{"start":481.68,"end":483.72,"text":"She's just left."},{"start":483.72,"end":487.48,"text":"Just goes between the auxiliary verb have or has"},{"start":487.48,"end":489.24,"text":"and the main verb."},{"start":489.24,"end":493.08,"text":"We also use the present perfect for things that happened in the past but have a"},{"start":493.08,"end":495.0,"text":"present result."},{"start":495.0,"end":496.52,"text":"He can't play today."},{"start":496.52,"end":498.44,"text":"He's twisted his ankle."},{"start":498.44,"end":501.4,"text":"As well as ever, never, and just,"},{"start":501.4,"end":504.56,"text":"we often use the present perfect with already"},{"start":504.56,"end":505.84,"text":"and yet."},{"start":505.84,"end":508.4,"text":"Already is used in positive sentences"},{"start":508.4,"end":513.12,"text":"to show that something happened before now. Yet is used in questions"},{"start":513.12,"end":514.32,"text":"and negatives"},{"start":514.32,"end":516.72,"text":"to show something has not happened"},{"start":516.72,"end":518.88,"text":"but we expected it to."},{"start":518.88,"end":520.68,"text":"As in, Carlos"},{"start":520.68,"end":521.8,"text":"has already"},{"start":521.8,"end":522.92,"text":"the report"},{"start":522.92,"end":525.52,"text":"but he hasn't shown it to the boss yet."},{"start":525.52,"end":527.48,"text":"Already goes between the auxiliary"},{"start":527.48,"end":529.04,"text":"and the main verb."},{"start":529.04,"end":532.0,"text":"Yet goes at the end of the sentence."},{"start":532.0,"end":536.12,"text":"We also use the present perfect for something that started in the past"},{"start":536.12,"end":538.0,"text":"and is still true now."},{"start":538.0,"end":541.6,"text":"We've known each other since we were children."},{"start":541.6,"end":546.36,"text":"Or Sam hasn't worked here for at least 3 years."},{"start":546.36,"end":550.52,"text":"Make sure you use for to indicate the period of time"},{"start":550.52,"end":551.84,"text":"and since"},{"start":551.84,"end":554.0,"text":"for when it started."},{"start":554.0,"end":556.28,"text":"How long have you had that phone?"},{"start":556.28,"end":558.52,"text":"I've had it for 8 months"},{"start":558.52,"end":560.44,"text":"since last Christmas."},{"start":560.44,"end":566.16,"text":"Okay, let's move on to our final present tense, the present perfect continuous."},{"start":566.16,"end":567.92,"text":"I've been teaching."},{"start":567.92,"end":568.64,"text":"Use"},{"start":568.64,"end":570.84,"text":"have been or has been"},{"start":570.84,"end":573.12,"text":"plus the verb in ing"},{"start":573.12,"end":575.08,"text":"to make this tense."},{"start":575.08,"end":577.12,"text":"We use the present perfect continuous"},{"start":577.12,"end":580.64,"text":"to describe actions that began in the past"},{"start":580.64,"end":581.68,"text":"and continue"},{"start":581.68,"end":583.08,"text":"up to the present."},{"start":583.08,"end":583.92,"text":"Sometimes"},{"start":583.92,"end":587.28,"text":"the meaning is the same as the present perfect simple."},{"start":587.28,"end":588.56,"text":"For example,"},{"start":588.56,"end":591.24,"text":"I've worked here for 6 years."},{"start":591.24,"end":595.56,"text":"I've been working here for 6 years. The same. Miguel's"},{"start":595.56,"end":598.32,"text":"played the guitar since he was three."},{"start":598.32,"end":599.16,"text":"Miguel's"},{"start":599.16,"end":601.8,"text":"been playing the guitar since he was three."},{"start":601.8,"end":603.08,"text":"The same."},{"start":603.08,"end":605.96,"text":"We tend to use the present perfect continuous"},{"start":605.96,"end":607.56,"text":"when we want to emphasize"},{"start":607.56,"end":608.68,"text":"the duration"},{"start":608.68,"end":610.56,"text":"of an activity."},{"start":610.56,"end":611.6,"text":"Ugh,"},{"start":611.6,"end":614.96,"text":"I've been waiting in this queue for hours"},{"start":614.96,"end":616.76,"text":"and I'm still waiting."},{"start":616.76,"end":618.8,"text":"Or they've been dancing"},{"start":618.8,"end":622.12,"text":"all night long and they're still dancing."},{"start":622.12,"end":624.72,"text":"We generally use the present perfect continuous"},{"start":624.72,"end":626.72,"text":"to focus on the action"},{"start":626.72,"end":628.72,"text":"and the present perfect simple"},{"start":628.72,"end":630.92,"text":"to focus on the result."},{"start":630.92,"end":633.16,"text":"Let's compare. Oh, Jessica,"},{"start":633.16,"end":635.0,"text":"what have you done?"},{"start":635.0,"end":636.32,"text":"I'm sorry."},{"start":636.32,"end":638.12,"text":"I've burnt the pizza."},{"start":638.12,"end":639.2,"text":"The focus"},{"start":639.2,"end":641.08,"text":"is on the result of the action."},{"start":641.08,"end":643.56,"text":"Or what have you been doing this afternoon,"},{"start":643.56,"end":644.96,"text":"Jessica?"},{"start":644.96,"end":648.4,"text":"I've been baking a cake for mom's birthday."},{"start":648.4,"end":651.88,"text":"Here, the focus is on the action, the activity."},{"start":651.88,"end":654.56,"text":"And notice that with the present perfect continuous,"},{"start":654.56,"end":658.72,"text":"we don't know if Jessica has finished baking or not."},{"start":658.72,"end":663.44,"text":"With the present perfect simple, the action is definitely completed."},{"start":663.44,"end":667.32,"text":"This tense is often used to explain the cause of something."},{"start":667.32,"end":668.6,"text":"For example,"},{"start":668.6,"end":670.56,"text":"why are you so tired?"},{"start":670.56,"end":674.36,"text":"Because I've been working a lot of overtime this week."},{"start":674.36,"end":677.4,"text":"And remember to use the present perfect simple,"},{"start":677.4,"end":679.04,"text":"not the continuous,"},{"start":679.04,"end":680.48,"text":"with state verbs."},{"start":680.48,"end":681.92,"text":"I've always"},{"start":681.92,"end":682.64,"text":"loved"},{"start":682.64,"end":683.84,"text":"Switzerland,"},{"start":683.84,"end":684.56,"text":"not"},{"start":684.56,"end":687.32,"text":"I've always been loving Switzerland."},{"start":687.32,"end":692.04,"text":"And be careful with this common error. We use the present perfect continuous"},{"start":692.04,"end":693.36,"text":"or simple,"},{"start":693.36,"end":694.12,"text":"not"},{"start":694.12,"end":695.8,"text":"the present continuous"},{"start":695.8,"end":696.76,"text":"to ask"},{"start":696.76,"end":697.88,"text":"how long."},{"start":697.88,"end":701.04,"text":"How long have you been studying English?"},{"start":701.04,"end":704.16,"text":"Not how long are you studying English?"},{"start":704.16,"end":706.52,"text":"So, here's a quick recap."},{"start":706.52,"end":708.8,"text":"Use the present simple for facts,"},{"start":708.8,"end":710.8,"text":"habits, and routines."},{"start":710.8,"end":712.36,"text":"Use the present continuous"},{"start":712.36,"end":717.2,"text":"for things happening now or around now and for temporary situations."},{"start":717.2,"end":720.8,"text":"Use the present perfect simple to discuss life experiences"},{"start":720.8,"end":723.32,"text":"without specifying when they occurred,"},{"start":723.32,"end":725.72,"text":"how many times something has happened,"},{"start":725.72,"end":729.28,"text":"or recent and past events with present results."},{"start":729.28,"end":734.24,"text":"And use the present perfect continuous to focus on an action and its duration."},{"start":734.24,"end":737.4,"text":"Well, that brings us to the end of today's video lesson."},{"start":737.4,"end":742.4,"text":"I've included a mini quiz to test how much you've learned in the ebook, so don't"},{"start":742.4,"end":745.36,"text":"forget to download that. The QR code is there"},{"start":745.36,"end":749.6,"text":"and the link is in the description box. Remember, we cover all of the tenses in"},{"start":749.6,"end":752.4,"text":"the ebook. I will see you in the next video."},{"start":752.4,"end":754.57,"text":"Bye."},{"start":754.57,"end":755.37,"text":">>"}]}